  "description": "A vanishing craft economy is seen from inside its last practitioners. Elderly men and their beloved dogs slip into Piedmont forests at night for white truffles worth more than gold, while dealers in suits wait at the edge of the woods. Shot like a Renaissance painting, scored by the men's own singing — competence, secrecy and interspecies partnership, all quietly ending.\n\nDeep in the forests of Piedmont, Italy, a handful of men, seventy or eighty years old, hunt for the rare and expensive white Alba truffle-which to date has resisted all of modern science's efforts at cultivation.",
